import test from'node:test';import assert from'node:assert/strict';import *as fs from'node:fs';import *as path from'node:path';import *as crypto from'node:crypto';import *as util from'node:util';import{SourceTextModule,SyntheticModule,createContext}from'node:vm';import{pathToFileURL,fileURLToPath}from'node:url';import{repo,root}from'./guard.mjs';
const area=path.resolve(repo,'work/resume/task04-model-drift-native-preparation-c3/extension/runtime-proof-'+crypto.randomUUID());fs.mkdirSync(area,{mode:0o700});const digest=b=>crypto.createHash('sha256').update(b).digest('hex');
async function context(sourceOverride){const base=path.resolve(area,crypto.randomUUID()),packet=path.resolve(base,'a/b/c/d');fs.mkdirSync(path.resolve(packet,'scripts'),{recursive:true,mode:0o700});fs.mkdirSync(path.resolve(packet,'fixture'),{mode:0o700});const put=(name,value)=>fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(packet,name),typeof value==='string'?value:JSON.stringify(value)+'\n');const external=[['parent.mjs','parent-source'],['watcher.mjs','watcher-source']].map(([name,body])=>{fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(base,name),body);return{path:name,bytes:Buffer.byteLength(body),sha256:digest(body)};});fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(base,'accepted.ts'),'accepted');fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(base,'product.ts'),'product');const source=sourceOverride??fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(root,'scripts/guard.mjs'),'utf8');put('scripts/guard.mjs',source);for(const name of ['project-request.json','cases.json','registration-inventory.json','schema-evidence.json','profile.json','divergence.json','toolchain-evidence.json'])put(name,{});put('historical-preservation.json',{packets:[]});put('runtime-inputs.json',{externalSources:external});put('source-inventory.json',{acceptedGateHashes:[{path:'accepted.ts',sha256:digest('accepted')}],files:[{source:'product.ts',sha256:digest('product')}]});put('fixture/module.ts','fixture-source');put('history.txt','historical-evidence');const legacyRoots=['project-request.json','cases.json','source-inventory.json','registration-inventory.json','schema-evidence.json','profile.json','divergence.json','toolchain-evidence.json','runtime-inputs.json','historical-preservation.json'];const match=source.match(/export const runtimeRootInputs=Object.freeze\(\[([^\]]*)\]\)/),roots=match?[...match[1].matchAll(/'([^']+)'/g)].map(m=>m[1]):legacyRoots;for(const name of roots)if(!fs.existsSync(path.resolve(packet,name)))put(name,{});fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(base,'runner-runtime.js'),'runner');fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(base,'compiler-runtime.js'),'compiler');put('toolchain-evidence.json',{files:[{path:'compiler-runtime.js',sha256:digest('compiler')}]});put('runner-dependency-inventory.json',{inputs:[{path:'runner-runtime.js',bytes:6,sha256:digest('runner')}]});put('dependency-tiers.json',{rpc:{runner:[{path:'runner-runtime.js',bytes:6,sha256:digest('runner')}],tools:[]},boundaryOnly:{runner:[],tools:[{path:'compiler-runtime.js',sha256:digest('compiler')}]}});if(roots.includes('dependency-inventory.json'))put('dependency-inventory.json',{inputs:[]});const paths=['scripts/guard.mjs','fixture/module.ts',...roots].sort();const rec=name=>({path:name,bytes:fs.statSync(path.resolve(packet,name)).size,sha256:digest(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(packet,name)))});put('runtime-freeze.json',{operationalPaths:paths,files:paths.map(rec)});const manifest={files:[...paths,'history.txt','runtime-freeze.json'].sort().map(rec)};put('qa-manifest.json',manifest);const review={preservationManifestSHA256:digest(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(packet,'qa-manifest.json')))};const vmContext=createContext({process:{getuid:()=>process.getuid(),env:{}},Buffer,Date,setTimeout});const module=new SourceTextModule(source,{context:vmContext,identifier:path.resolve(packet,'scripts/guard.mjs'),initializeImportMeta:m=>m.url=pathToFileURL(path.resolve(packet,'scripts/guard.mjs')).href});const imports={'node:fs':fs,'node:path':path,'node:url':{fileURLToPath},'node:crypto':crypto,'node:util':util};await module.link(name=>{const obj=imports[name];assert.ok(obj);return new SyntheticModule(Object.keys(obj),function(){for(const[k,v]of Object.entries(obj))this.setExport(k,v);},{context:vmContext});});await module.evaluate();return{base,packet,module:module.namespace,review,put,expectedFiles:manifest.files.length,env:vmContext.process.env};}
test('actual unadapted guard runtime closure checks consumed divergence/toolchain/external sources each call; historical scans only explicit boundaries',async()=>{const h=await context();assert.ok(h.module.sourcePreflight());assert.equal(h.module.preservationPreflight(h.review).files,h.expectedFiles);h.put('history.txt','changed-history');assert.ok(h.module.sourcePreflight(),'historical-only evidence not runtime input');assert.throws(()=>h.module.preservationPreflight(h.review),/QA_PRESERVATION_DRIFT/);});
for(const name of ['divergence.json','toolchain-evidence.json'])test('actual runtime closure rejects changed '+name+' before effects',async()=>{const h=await context();h.put(name,{changed:true});assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight(),/QA_SOURCE_DRIFT/);});
test('actual runtime closure rejects canonical external parent and accepted/product source drift',async()=>{for(const[name,code]of [['parent.mjs','QA_EXTERNAL_SOURCE_DRIFT'],['watcher.mjs','QA_EXTERNAL_SOURCE_DRIFT'],['accepted.ts','QA_ACCEPTED_SOURCE_DRIFT'],['product.ts','QA_PRODUCT_DRIFT']]){const h=await context();fs.appendFileSync(path.resolve(h.base,name),'drift');assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight(),new RegExp(code));}});
test('actual preservation rejects manifest substitution and runtime inventory additions',async()=>{const h=await context();h.put('qa-manifest.json',{files:[]});assert.throws(()=>h.module.preservationPreflight(h.review),/QA_PRESERVATION_MANIFEST/);h.put('scripts/extra.mjs','unexpected');assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight(),/QA_SOURCE_INVENTORY_DRIFT/);});

test('actual historical manifest order regression preserves old red and accepts exact unsorted historical sets without mutation',async()=>{const old=fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(repo,'_goals/convex-backend-runtime-2026-10-02/qa/task04-native-admission-fixture-c8/evidence/full-preservation01-failure/scripts--guard.mjs.text'),'utf8');for(const[version,source]of [['old',old],['fixed',undefined]]){const h=await context(source),directory=path.resolve(h.base,'history');fs.mkdirSync(directory);for(const n of ['a.txt','z.txt'])fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(directory,n),n);const previous={files:['z.txt','a.txt'].map(n=>({path:n,bytes:5,sha256:digest(n)}))},body=JSON.stringify(previous)+'\n';fs.writeFileSync(path.resolve(directory,'manifest.json'),body);h.put('historical-preservation.json',{packets:[{path:'history',manifest:'manifest.json',manifestSHA256:digest(body),rows:2}]});const freeze=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'runtime-freeze.json')));for(const row of freeze.files)if(row.path==='historical-preservation.json'){const data=fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,row.path));row.bytes=data.length;row.sha256=digest(data);}h.put('runtime-freeze.json',freeze);const manifest=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'qa-manifest.json')));for(const row of manifest.files){const data=fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,row.path));row.bytes=data.length;row.sha256=digest(data);}h.put('qa-manifest.json',manifest);h.review.preservationManifestSHA256=digest(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'qa-manifest.json')));if(version==='old')assert.throws(()=>h.module.preservationPreflight(h.review),/QA_PRESERVATION_INVENTORY/);else assert.equal(h.module.preservationPreflight(h.review).historicalPackets,1);assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(directory,'manifest.json'),'utf8'),body);}});

for(const name of ['runner-runtime.js','compiler-runtime.js'])test('actual root loader/compiler source drift rejects before dispatch '+name,async()=>{const h=await context();fs.appendFileSync(path.resolve(h.base,name),'drift');assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight(),/QA_RUNNER_DEPENDENCY_DRIFT/);});

test('exact tier permits only unused compiler drift at RPC; full publication/final/unknown entry rejects',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);assert.ok(h.module.reviewed());fs.appendFileSync(path.resolve(h.base,'compiler-runtime.js'),'drift');assert.ok(h.module.sourcePreflight('rpc'));assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight(),/QA_RUNNER_DEPENDENCY_DRIFT/);assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight('unknown'),/QA_RUNNER_DEPENDENCY_DRIFT/);});
test('actual consumed runtime source drift rejects at RPC tier',async()=>{const h=await context();assert.ok(h.module.sourcePreflight());fs.appendFileSync(path.resolve(h.base,'runner-runtime.js'),'drift');assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight('rpc'),/QA_RUNNER_DEPENDENCY_DRIFT/);});
test('freeze substitution after first exact baseline rejects even same parsed fields',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);assert.ok(h.module.reviewed());assert.ok(h.module.sourcePreflight());fs.appendFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'runtime-freeze.json'),' ');assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight('rpc'),/QA_FREEZE_SUBSTITUTION/);});

function approval(h){fs.mkdirSync(h.module.scratch,{recursive:true,mode:0o700});const value={independent:true,verdict:'PASS',freezeSha256:digest(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'runtime-freeze.json'))),preservationManifestSHA256:h.review.preservationManifestSHA256};const file=path.resolve(h.module.scratch,'preparation-review.json');fs.writeFileSync(file,JSON.stringify(value)+'\n',{mode:0o600});h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256=digest(fs.readFileSync(file));return{value,file};}
test('first full reviewed baseline rejects freeze changed before external approved binding',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);fs.appendFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'runtime-freeze.json'),' ');assert.throws(()=>h.module.reviewed('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW/);});
test('full reviewed external pin fixes baseline and later review substitution rejects',async()=>{const h=await context(),a=approval(h);assert.ok(h.module.reviewed());assert.ok(h.module.reviewed('rpc'));fs.appendFileSync(a.file,' ');assert.throws(()=>h.module.reviewed('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW_SUBSTITUTION/);});

function coherent(h){h.put('fixture/module.ts','DUMMY-coherent-substitution');const frozen=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'runtime-freeze.json')));for(const row of frozen.files){const bytes=fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,row.path));row.bytes=bytes.length;row.sha256=digest(bytes);}h.put('runtime-freeze.json',frozen);fs.mkdirSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'nested'),{recursive:true});h.put('nested/qa-manifest.json',{files:[]});const walk=(dir=h.packet,prefix='')=>fs.readdirSync(dir,{withFileTypes:true}).flatMap(e=>e.isDirectory()?walk(path.resolve(dir,e.name),prefix+e.name+'/'):[prefix+e.name]).sort();h.put('qa-manifest.json',{files:walk().filter(n=>n!=='qa-manifest.json').map(n=>{const bytes=fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,n));return{path:n,bytes:bytes.length,sha256:digest(bytes)};})});h.review.preservationManifestSHA256=digest(fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(h.packet,'qa-manifest.json')));const expected=h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256;approval(h);h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256=expected;}
for(const [name,pin]of [['missing',undefined],['bad-format','A'.repeat(64)],['wrong','0'.repeat(64)]])test('ROOT external '+name+' expected pin denies before source/trusted/effects',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256=pin;h.put('runtime-freeze.json','INVALID_FREEZE_NOT_READ');assert.throws(()=>h.module.reviewed('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW_EXPECTED/);});
test('coherent operational+FULLfreeze+recursiveCOMPLETEmanifest+private review before FIRSTcall denied under original external pin',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);coherent(h);assert.throws(()=>h.module.reviewed('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW_EXPECTED_DIGEST/);assert.equal(h.module.preservationPreflight(h.review).files,h.expectedFiles+1);});
test('failed initial expected review cannot seed trusted binding; restored correct receipt passes',async()=>{const h=await context(),a=approval(h),bytes=fs.readFileSync(a.file);fs.appendFileSync(a.file,' ');assert.throws(()=>h.module.reviewed('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW_EXPECTED_DIGEST/);fs.writeFileSync(a.file,bytes);assert.ok(h.module.reviewed());});
test('later external environment pin drift denies reduced RPC validation and reviewed entry',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);assert.ok(h.module.reviewed());h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256='0'.repeat(64);assert.throws(()=>h.module.reviewed('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW_EXPECTED_PIN_DRIFT/);assert.throws(()=>h.module.sourcePreflight('rpc'),/QA_REVIEW_EXPECTED_PIN_DRIFT/);});

test('actual ProcessOwner entry blocks missing/wrong pin without spawn; healthy owned child propagates exact ROOT pin',async()=>{for(const mode of['missing','wrong','healthy','conflicting-child']){const h=await context();approval(h);if(mode==='missing')delete h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256;if(mode==='wrong')h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256='0'.repeat(64);let calls=0,received;const c=createContext({process:{execPath:'DUMMY',env:h.env},setTimeout});const source=fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(root,'scripts/process-owner.mjs'),'utf8');const mod=new SourceTextModule(source,{context:c});const ports={'./guard.mjs':{reviewed:h.module.reviewed,reviewPin:h.module.reviewPin},'node:child_process':{spawn:(_exe,_args,options)=>{calls++;received=options.env;return{once(){}};}},'./process-terminal.mjs':{linuxGroupMembers(){throw Error('NO_ACTUAL_PROCESS');},terminal(){throw Error('NO_ACTUAL_PROCESS');}}};await mod.link(n=>{const obj=ports[n];assert.ok(obj);return new SyntheticModule(Object.keys(obj),function(){for(const[k,v]of Object.entries(obj))this.setExport(k,v);},{context:c});});await mod.evaluate();const owner=new mod.namespace.ProcessOwner(),options={env:{PATH:'DUMMY'}};if(mode==='conflicting-child')options.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256='0'.repeat(64);if(mode==='healthy'){owner.spawn(['DUMMY'],options);assert.equal(calls,1);assert.equal(received.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256,h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256);assert.equal(owner.spawned,1);}else{assert.throws(()=>owner.spawn(['DUMMY'],options),/QA_(REVIEW_EXPECTED|CHILD_REVIEW_PIN)/);assert.equal(calls,0);assert.equal(owner.spawned,0);assert.equal(owner.records.size,0);}}});

test('missing external pin denies actual budget ticket before lock/window/ticket effects',async()=>{const h=await context();approval(h);delete h.env.CORTEX_QA_TASK04_REVIEW_SHA256;const before=fs.readdirSync(h.module.scratch).sort();await assert.rejects(()=>h.module.reserveTicket('native',h.module.limits.nativeClientRpc),/QA_REVIEW_EXPECTED_PIN/);assert.deepEqual(fs.readdirSync(h.module.scratch).sort(),before);});
